course: dictionary
lesson: 4904
title: Short forms and word pieces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer name or phrase. ILO is one. It stands for the International Labour Organization, a part of the United Nations that sets fair rules for work. Each capital letter comes from the first letter of a word in the full name.
explain: Use the words around a short form to work out what it means. «The ILO says children should be at school, not working.» The sentence says the ILO makes a statement about children and work, so it must be a group or an organisation, not a sound or a food.
explain: Some letters are only a piece of a longer word. «Ilo» on its own is not an English word. It appears inside kilo and silo. In the sentence «In Ilo, -ko turns a doing word into the person who does it», Ilo is the name of a made-up language, and the sentence explains how its word endings work.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a longer word or name.
fact: «ILO» stands for the International Labour Organization.
fact: The ILO is part of the United Nations and sets fair rules for work.
fact: The ILO says children should be at school, not working.
fact: «Ilo» on its own is not an English word; it is only a piece of words like kilo and silo.
exercise: «The ILO says children should be at school, not working.» What does ILO stand for? | International Lunch Order | Irish Land Office | Index of Local Oceans | *International Labour Organization
exercise: «Ilo» on its own is what kind of thing in English? | A short name for a child | A famous city in Geneva | A type of work | *Not an English word, only a piece of a longer word
exercise: Which word contains the piece «ilo»? | apple | orange | *silo | bench
test: What is an abbreviation? | A kind of fish | A sound a dog makes | *A short form of a longer name or phrase | A long story with many chapters
test: In «In Ilo, -ko turns dami into damiko», what does -ko do? | Makes a word mean no | Turns a word into a question | Makes a noun plural | *Turns a doing word into the person who does it
exam: Which of these is an abbreviation? | *ILO | kilo | wheel | silo
